{"id":"n1t","type":"text","x":1024,"y":232,"width":852,"height":200,"angle":0,"strokeColor":"#1e1e1e","backgroundColor":"transparent","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":1,"strokeStyle":"solid","roughness":0,"opacity":100,"groupIds":[],"roundness":null,"seed":133,"version":1,"isDeleted":false,"boundElements":null,"updated":1730000000000,"text":"Why it works: particles tag each word's job, so the blocks can move — the verb is the only fixed anchor.\n\n• 私はリンゴを食べる。 = I eat an apple.\n• リンゴを私は食べる。 = still correct (emphatic)!\n• (私は)食べる。 = subjects drop out when obvious.\n• Questions need no reordering — just add か: 食べますか？","fontSize":16,"fontFamily":2,"textAlign":"left","verticalAlign":"top","containerId":null,"originalText":"Why it works: particles tag each word's job, so the blocks can move — the verb is the only fixed anchor.\n\n• 私はリンゴを食べる。 = I eat an apple.\n• リンゴを私は食べる。 = still correct (emphatic)!\n• (私は)食べる。 = subjects drop out when obvious.\n• Questions need no reordering — just add か: 食べますか？","lineHeight":1.25},
